{"type":"assistant","message":{"model":"claude-opus-4-6","id":"msg_011CfgTpAb4rte3amWTxNdu5","type":"message","role":"assistant","content":[{"type":"text","text":"I see the bug. In `publish()`, the date is stored as the UTC date, not the author's local date. An author in Tokyo posting at 1 AM local time (which is 4 PM UTC the previous day) gets yesterday's date. And `display_date()` tries to re-convert the stored date to the viewer's timezone, which can also flip the day.\n\nThe fix: store the date in the author's timezone, and return it as-is in `display_date` (a post's date is a fixed fact — it shouldn't shift per viewer)."}],"container":null,"stop_reason":null,"stop_sequence":null,"stop_details":null,"usage":{"input_tokens":1,"cache_creation_input_tokens":1315,"cache_read_input_tokens":25136,"cache_creation":{"ephemeral_5m_input_tokens":0,"ephemeral_1h_input_tokens":1315},"output_tokens":9,"service_tier":"standard","inference_geo":"not_available"},"input_transformations":[],"diagnostics":null,"context_management":null},"parent_tool_use_id":null,"session_id":"c220608f-b262-4df6-846d-c7e5e2b20929","uuid":"3b17dfb0-f482-4ad7-aa67-e428650f4f48","timestamp":"2026-10-04T03:11:10.601Z","request_id":"req_011CfgTpAKgszxMF4D5Zh5TE"}
